From 4def68877eb0c40c397a6575686cef6f7a008dc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Pacheco <alepacheco99@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:27:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 74/89] Properly verify RPCSEC_GSS call arguments

In gssrpc__svcauth_gss(), use a new helper svcauth_gss_check_call()
for RPCSEC_GSS_DATA and RPCSEC_GSS_DESTROY() messages, subsuming the
existing sequence number checking and svcauth_gss_validate() calls.
In the helper, set gd->sec.svc to the verified service value
(typically RPCSEC_GSS_SVC_PRIVACY) from the current message, to be
used when unwrapping call arguments and wrapping return arguments.
Check the sequence number before the verifier, and check the verifier
before updating the sequence window.

In svcauth_gss_accept_sec_context(), do not record the unverified
service value.

Add an RPCSEC_GSS mode to the gssrpc unit-test client.  In this mode,
make a call at each service level after establishing the context at
each level.

[ghudson@mit.edu: edited commit message; made minor style edits]

CVE-2026-118380:

In MIT krb5 release 1.4 and later, an active network attacker can
alter the arguments sent by a legitimate client to RPC services
protected by RPCSEC_GSS, or cause return values to be sent in plain
text.

ticket: 9272 (new)
tags: pullup
target_version: 1.22-next

(cherry picked from commit 448c78373984c752500a3197256b99cca7fa1d1e)
